+## 6j. Task 15: membrane propagation loss 0.1–3 dB/cm (R 95 %, 3.3 µm)
+
+`scripts/t15_loss.py` → `results/t15/summary.json`, `results/t15/table.md` (run commands in its docstring). Task 14 design and
+model at R 95 %, slab-mode loss 0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 1, 2, 3 dB/cm; M calibrated per loss against new Task 2 engine runs
+(`results/t2/circle_mir_R0.95_<dB>dB.json`; c_cal 1.425, 1.540, 1.672, 1.716, 1.948, 2.382); Herriott of the same length for
+comparison. 100 ms limits with `scripts/t14_milestones.py` (period-locked, referenced, 14 pW/√Hz, + 8 dB couplers).
+
+- Γ⟨L⟩ of the light that reaches the detector falls slowly (10 mm: 12.0, 11.1, 10.4, 8.4, 5.7, 4.5 cm), but the transmission falls
+  exponentially with the ≈ 20 cm mean path (10 mm: 6.9, 2.6, 1.1, 0.18, 0.0095, 0.00087 %). The limits follow the transmission:
+  10 mm, 10 mW, CH₄ / C₂H₆ at 100 ms: 0.74 / 0.94, 2.05 / 2.59, 5.2 / 6.6, 40 / 51, 930 / 1180, 1.3e4 / 1.6e4 ppb.
+- The best cell size shrinks with the loss: 20 mm at 0.1 dB/cm (0.41 / 0.52 ppb at 10 mW), 10 mm at 0.3, 5 mm at 0.5 (4.0 / 5.1)
+  and 1 dB/cm (10.5 / 13.3; 4.2 / 5.3 at 30 mW). At ≥ 2 dB/cm no cell of 5–20 mm reaches 10 ppb at 100 ms with ≤ 30 mW.
+- Static fringe with all dithers stays below 5e-7 up to 0.5 dB/cm in all cells and up to 1 dB/cm at 5–10 mm; at 2–3 dB/cm the
+  short paths leave fewer grains (6.7e-7 – 8.8e-6). Insertion loss ≤ 25 dB (M4): 10 mm up to 0.3 dB/cm, 5 mm up to 0.5 dB/cm.
+- Herriott (10 mm) loses less (T 50 → 2.3 %, its paths are 2–4 cm) but keeps Γ⟨L⟩ 2.2–4.0 cm and 1.3–1.8e-6 fringe.
+- Proposal check: M2 (≤ 0.3 dB/cm, target 0.1) and the RO2 failure criterion (> 0.5 dB/cm) bracket the range where the CMPC meets
+  M3, M4 and M7; R2.1's "the 25 dB case tolerates R = 90 % and 1 dB/cm" is not supported by this design at R 95 % (5 mm, 1 dB/cm:
+  27.5 dB), although M7 at 100 ms is still reachable there with 10–30 mW.
+
